    "body": "EICMA 2026 • Benelli Showed the World Its New Tornado Naked Tre 903 Concept at EICMA 2026 and It's a Triple!\nBYD Integrates Solar Power, Energy Storage, Flash Charging, Robotic Charging System Into a Facility\n7 photos\nPhoto: BYD\nBYD , the multinational high-tech company established in 1994 with the clear goal of pursuing Tesla's place of world EV dominance, is taking a new step toward the path of becoming an all-in-one provider of new energy ‘greatness.’\nThe Chinese brand was initially a rechargeable battery maker, but a little more than three decades later it has invested in automobiles, rail transit, new energy, and electronics, with over 30 industrial parks in China, the United States, Canada, Japan, Brazil, Hungary, and India. BYD Auto was founded a little later, in 2003, but through “significant technological advancements” like the Blade Battery , the DM-i and DM-p hybrid technology, or the Super e-Platform, it has quickly risen the ranks to become the world’s largest EV maker since 2025.\nNow, BYD has announced the creation of a new installation in the Abu Dhabi desert that features a new type of integrated charging system, “bringing together solar power generation, energy storage, Flash Charging and robotic charging for the first time in a single solution.” The system aims to mix the use and generation of renewable energy with the company’s proprietary ultra-fast charging and automated vehicle technology, thus establishing a new type of approach to the charging experience.\nThe station has BYD’s Flash Charging technology, which enables charging times to move closer than ever to conventional refueling, with the time needed to go from 10% to 70% state-of-charge being an advertised five minutes, followed by a potential 10% to 97% in nine minutes. The new integrated system combines the proprietary Flash Charging station with solar power generation, energy storage, and even robotic charging.\nMore precisely, the installation uses BYD’s Solar-Storage-Charging (SSC) system, which links solar energy generation to battery storage and Flash Charging. Basically, the local solar energy is captured and stored on-site to be used for vehicle charging as needed. The SSC supports independent operation from the grid, opening up flexibility in locations where grid access is limited.\nOf course, BYD took the new SSC installation to the Abu Dhabi desert, where the climate is a haven for solar charging – the area is characterized “by intense sunlight, high temperatures and scarce rainfall.” Additionally, the system integrates a robotic arm that can take care of the vehicle’s charging connection, “automatically locating the charging port, opening its cover and inserting the connector.”\nIt uses both visual guidance and force feedback so that the arm can ensure accurate alignment and a secure connection to BYD’s Flash Charging system. Additionally, BYD wants to integrate the robotic charging with Automated Valet Parking, so that “drivers can simply exit the vehicle, lock it, and walk away while the car autonomously navigates to a designated charging space,” where the robotic arm takes over to connect the vehicle and start the charging process.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nBYD flash charging Blade Battery solar power energy storage SSC Solar-Storage-Charging robot\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT This Is What the Facelifted 2028 BMW M5 Will Look Like – Rendering",
